      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I've broken down each topic into a detailed module structure, focusing on high granularity while maintaining pedagogical soundness. This approach ensures that the syllabus is logical and useful, rather than just inflating the Granularity Score.\n\n**Module 1: Qubits and Superposition**\n\n1.1. Introduction to Qubits\n\t* Definition and properties of qubits\n\t* Comparison with classical bits\n\t* Visualizing qubits using Bloch spheres\n1.2. Superposition Fundamentals\n\t* Mathematical representation of superposition\n\t* Visualizing superposition using wave functions\n\t* Implications of superposition on quantum computing\n1.3. Superposition Applications\n\t* Quantum parallelism and speedup\n\t* Quantum teleportation and entanglement\n\t* Quantum computing with superposition\n\n**Module 2: Quantum Entanglement**\n\n2.1. Entanglement Basics\n\t* Definition and properties of entanglement\n\t* Mathematical representation of entanglement\n\t* Visualizing entanglement using Bell states\n2.2. Entanglement Applications\n\t* Quantum teleportation and quantum cryptography\n\t* Quantum computing with entanglement\n\t* Entanglement swapping and quantum",
      "source": "target",
